Package: c-backup
Version: 0.10.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6, libssl3, liblz4-1, libacl1, libsqlite3-0, libmicrohttpd12, libcurl4, systemd
Maintainer: XxI0NICxX <vifair22@gmail.com>
Description: Content-addressed backup daemon
 One daemon per machine, owning every repository on it. Content-addressed
 storage with LZ4 compression, Reed-Solomon parity, sparse-file handling and
 pack coalescing, exposed over an HTTP API on a unix socket and a TCP port.
 .
 Repositories are self-describing: manifest trees stored alongside the data
 mean the index can be rebuilt from a repository at any time, so losing the
 daemon database costs time rather than backups.
